From ae98c7dc85eff37780e385585ae8c319f1a8f356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:18:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAESink: a pause of passthrough gives back what it had
 not written

What the sink needs for a pause of passthrough that keeps its sound, for a
stream that it packs into IEC 61937 itself (the engine asks for it in the
next commit; nothing here runs before that):

- HOLD: the packets it has not written go back to the engine as a flush
  has them, but marked unwritten (RETURNUNWRITTEN), in their order, and
  the answer says what the device holds, which plays out. The sink answers
  between two writes, so a packet comes back whole or has been written
  whole: no burst is cut.
- While that pause lasts, the silence that keeps the device alive goes out
  as IEC 61937 pause bursts. Kodi sends pause bursts only while a stream
  plays and zeros otherwise, which a receiver takes for the end of the
  bitstream: the sound after the pause has to be locked onto again, and a
  TrueHD decoder starts again at the next major sync. Pause bursts are what
  a correction of the sync already sends in the middle of a stream. The
  silence is kept three frames under the size of the device, so that at
  the resume the device never holds more silence than the sound that
  played after the picture stopped (HeldSilenceWaitMs()).
- RESUMEGAP: at the resume a pause goes before the next packet written:
  the sound that played with the picture stopped, less what the picture
  moved since and what the device holds then, so that the sound goes on
  where the picture is (GapMs()); in pauses of a frame at most, as a
  correction of the sync has them.
- HOLDDROPPED: what the engine kept at the pause was let go (a seek, a
  stop, the output opened again): the silence goes out as after a pause
  that keeps nothing. The packer is reset for it: PackPause() re-uses
  its last pause of the same length whatever it is asked for, and would
  send the pause bursts on. A stream that streams again, a flush and a
  change of the output end such a pause too.

The pause bursts are packed by CAEBitstreamPacker::PackPause() as before.
The decision between pause bursts and zeros is the same expression as
before when no such pause is held (AsBursts()): PCM, a pause that does not
keep the sound and a sink that takes the stream unpacked are as before.

TestPassthroughPause: the reckoning (clock, gap, silence, what is kept),
and what goes out around such a pause for AC-3, E-AC-3, TrueHD (MAT) and
DTS-HD MA, every buffer a valid IEC 61937 burst or valid pause bursts.
